activation	Print prompt	2026-10-28T03:56:33.9318255Z {"title": "SIGSEGV when executing an ASOF join with a non-comparison condition", "body": "### What happens?\n\nExecuting an ASOF join whose `ON` clause contains a non-comparison conjunct crashes with SIGSEGV when the optimizer is disabled. `EXPLAIN` of the same query works, and with the optimizer enabled the query runs fine - the crash only happens when a query is actually executed under `SET debug_disable_optimizer=true`. I hit this while testing upstream reference  number 26292, whose disable_optimizer CI run surfaces it through a new ASOF join test.\n\nThe crash is in the ASOF nested-loop planning path added by upstream reference  number 16218: `PlanAsOfLoopJoin` estimates the cardinality of the join subtree after its children were already planned, and planning a child scan consumes its bind data, so the estimate dereferences a null bind data pointer in `TableScanCardinality`. The table contents and types do not matter - any non-comparison condition (e.g. an `IN` list) triggers it.\n\n### To Reproduce\n\n```sql\nSET debug_disable_optimizer=true;\nCREATE TABLE a_t AS SELECT (range % 3)::INTEGER AS k, ['sad', 'ok', 'happy'][1 + range % 3] AS m, range::INTEGER AS t FROM range(12);\nCREATE TABLE b_t AS SELECT (range % 3)::INTEGER AS k, range::INTEGER AS t FROM range(12);\nSELECT count(*)\nFROM a_t ASOF JOIN b_t\n    ON a_t.k = b_t.k AND a_t.t >= b_t.t AND a_t.m IN ('sad', 'ok', 'happy');\n```\n\nOutput (the process crashes before producing any result):\n\n```text\nzsh: segmentation fault  duckdb < repro.sql\n```\n\nThe crash stack (from a reldebug build), showing the null bind data reaching the scan's cardinality callback:\n\n```text\n* frame #0: duckdb::TableScanCardinality(context=..., bind_data_p=0x0000000000000000) at table_scan.cpp:1133\n    frame #1: duckdb::LogicalGet::EstimateCardinality at logical_get.cpp:310\n    frame #3: duckdb::LogicalOperator::EstimateCardinality\n    frame #4: duckdb::PhysicalPlanGenerator::PlanAsOfLoopJoin at plan_asof_join.cpp:259\n    frame #5: duckdb::PhysicalPlanGenerator::PlanAsOfJoin at plan_asof_join.cpp:357\n```\n\nObservations that pin it down:\n\n- Without the non-comparison conjunct (`a_t.m IN (...)` removed) the query plans and runs fine.\n- `EXPLAIN` of the crashing query does not crash - with the optimizer disabled, nothing caches an estimate on the operators, which is exactly the state in which the post-planning estimate touches the consumed bind data.\n- With the optimizer enabled (default) the query also runs fine, because the statistics propagation has already cached cardinalities on every operator.\n\n### OS:\n\nmacOS 26.5 arm64\n\n### DuckDB Version:\n\nv2.0.0-dev86171\n\n### DuckDB Client:\n\nCLI\n\n### Hardware:\n\n_No response_\n\n### Full Name:\n\nJaySon Huang\n\n### Affiliation:\n\nPingCAP\n\n### Did you include all relevant configuration (e.g., CPU architecture, Linux distribution) to reproduce the issue?\n\n- [x] Yes, I have\n\n### Did you include all code required to reproduce the issue?\n\n- [x] Yes, I have\n\n### Did you include all relevant data sets for reproducing the issue?\n\nNot applicable - the reproduction does not require a data set"}
